# NOTE: plots/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It holds source (plot_*.py) as well as the thesis
# figures, which are a deliverable and small (~2 MB). Ignoring the whole directory silently
# excluded newly added scripts/figures — git only applies ignore rules to UNtracked files, so
# already-tracked ones kept working and hid the problem.
# Superseded figure sets generated BEFORE the PPO/PT corrections (see FINDINGS.md §3): kept on
# disk for reference but not committed, so stale numbers can't be mistaken for results.
plots/figures_multitask_all5seeds/
plots/figures_singletask/
plots/vanilla_before_after.png
wandb/
videos/
*.pt
*.pkl
*.log

# ---- Derived data / exports ----
numeric_logs_csv/
numeric_logs_csv.zip

# ---- Knowledge-graph / tooling output ----
graphify-out/

# Keep source configs, README, requirements, scripts, and code tracked.
# To force-track a specific artifact (e.g. a paper figure): git add -f plots/final.png
